# bar: at least as readable as the hand-written diagnostic this replaces.
# The user's mistake is on this line; the message must not point into
# `src/std/list.cn` or talk about `list::from_array`'s `T`.
#
# Phase 8 changed what this message can honestly say. `[]` is now pinned by
# a later use, so the old text — "the element type is not inferred from a
# later `push`" — became false. The message now names the uses that would
# have pinned it and says none of them happen here, which is the difference
# between a rule and a fact about this function.
module infer_diag.empty_list_literal

def wrong() -> unit:
    var xs = []
